00:44:12,631 --> 00:44:18,631
Ron Howard is an American director, producer, screenwriter, and actor.

11
00:48:37,894 --> 00:48:43,894
He started his career portraying Opie, the son of Andy Taylor (played by Andy Griffith) in the sitcom The Andy Griffith Show
from 1960 through 1968 and Richie Cunningham in the sitcom Happy Days, a role he would play from 1974 to 1980.

12
00:53:03,157 --> 00:53:09,157
During this time, he also acted in films such as The Music Man
(1962), American Graffiti (1973), and The Shootist (1976).

13
00:57:28,421 --> 00:57:34,421
Howard retired from acting in 1980.

14
01:01:53,684 --> 01:01:59,684
He then shifted into directing comedies such as Night Shift (1982), Splash (1984), and Cocoon (1985) as well as
the fantasy Willow (1988), the thriller Backdraft (1991), and the newspaper film The Paper (1994).

15
01:06:18,947 --> 01:06:24,947
He then transitioned into directing critically acclaimed dramas such as Apollo 13 (1995), A Beautiful Mind
(2001), Cinderella Man (2005), Frost/Nixon (2008), Rush (2013), and In the Heart of the Sea (2015).

16
01:10:44,210 --> 01:10:50,210
Howard also directed the children's film How the Grinch Stole Christmas (2000) as well as the Robert Langdon film
series, The Da Vinci Code (2006), Angels & Demons (2009), Inferno (2016), and Solo: A Star Wars Story (2018).

17
01:15:09,473 --> 01:15:15,473
He has also directed the documentary films The Beatles:
Eight Days a Week (2016) and Pavarotti (2019).

